   "file": "plugins/specclaw/hooks/register.tsx",
   "fp": "6c551808d9ba",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 10,
   "message": "`options.gate` is cast to `GateMode` without checking it. An empty string or an unknown value such as `Block` or `deny` passes `?? 'warn'` unchanged. It then reaches `held()`, where any value other than `warn` becomes `deny`, so the gate silently runs in block mode and nothing says the config was not recognised. The behaviour fails closed, which B6 allows, but the bad input is never flagged. Fix: validate the value against `['warn','block','off']` and toast once when it is not one of them, for example 'specclaw: unknown gate mode <x>, using block'. Add a test row for `''` and `'Block'`.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B6",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  }
 ],
